#@Comment Thickness of a powder pressed under a stiff window clamped at the rim (a bent plate): most of the area near the rim thickness.
#@Comment $P(X) \propto \frac{1}{\sqrt{X - d_e}}$ on $[d_e, d_c]$. {rim} - the rim thickness $d_e$. It is infinite at the rim, so start L half a step above it: L = $d_e + (d_c - d_e)/(2\,\mathrm{Num})$, R = $d_c$.
